  "id": "COMPOUND:2838 - PROTEIN:4930",
  "verbalization": "Patupilone is implicated in the biological pathway leading to the Small conductance calcium-activated potassium channel protein 1 through a series of targets, all of which are modulated by palmarumycin CP18. The evidence suggests that Patupilone acts as a target of palmarumycin CP18, which in turn affects the Small conductance calcium-activated potassium channel protein 1. This relationship is supported by multiple paths, each linking Patupilone to palmarumycin CP18 and then to the target protein. The consistent presence of palmarumycin CP18 as a common mediator across different targets indicates a potential mechanism of action involving this compound. The integration of these paths highlights a possible regulatory or functional link between Patupilone and the target protein, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
